## 0. Is there a real gap? Yes — and it is unusually well-specified

Not "nobody has studied web development." Something sharper, which the vault establishes by **absence**:

> **Mechanisms validated in general programming and data-science education have never been tested in a front-end / interface-layer cohort.**

The evidence for that claim is the vault itself:

| Vault source | Cohort studied | Front-end? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Garcia 2025 | 176 undergraduates, *web design and development course* (FEU, Manila) | ✅ **the only one** |
| Phung 2025 | 102 students, introductory **data science** programming | ❌ |
| Singh 2026 | **data science** education | ❌ |
| Kazemitabaar 2024 (CodeAid) | programming course, LLM assistant deployment | ❌ general |
| Liu, Fan & Pan 2026 | programming education, grounded theory | ❌ general |
| Parthasarathy & Joshi 2024 | **faculty** perceptions, India | ❌ not students |
| Batista 2025 · Correa 2025 | **websites** audited, not learners | ❌ not cohorts |

And `profield-frontend-pedagogy.md` already carries the matching tags: web-specific cognitive-offloading effect sizes `[UNVERIFIED-GAP]`; no settled sequencing model for 3D web in HE `[UNVERIFIED-GAP]`; no HE pedagogy source for the IoT/robotics *interface* layer `[UNVERIFIED-GAP]`; Python-backed interfaces `[UNVERIFIED-GAP]`.

**There is also no Spanish cohort anywhere in either vault.** Not one.

So the gap is not a hunch. It is a documented, queryable empty set — and you are already standing in it, teaching.

