## 1. Asset inventory — why *you*, and why now

Be honest about the advantage, because it is real but specific. You will not out-RCT a CER lab. You have something they cannot easily get:

| Asset | Why it is research-grade |
| --- | --- |
| **FE I annual (2nd yr) + FE II semester (3rd yr)** | A **longitudinal arc with the same students across two years** — rare, and the natural design for "what survives the framework." |
| **Two degrees share the subject** (Full-Stack + Ciencia de Datos e IA) | A **naturally occurring cross-group comparison** you did not have to construct. Directly tests interface-layer *transferability* — the field's open question. |
| **FE II is brand new** | A clean **pilot with no prior-year contamination**, and a legitimate design-based-research site. |
| **Assessment already instrumented** | AI-use declarations, commit narratives, decision/iteration logs, oral-defence rubric. **You are already generating the data**; it is simply not yet consented, structured, or analysed. |
| **Published, versioned curriculum** | The Web Atelier site + git history is a **reproducibility artefact** most practitioner papers cannot offer. |
| **Profield + Ahmes** | A systematic-review and provenance capability that is, frankly, ahead of the median CER practitioner paper. |
| **Sociologist collaborator** | Instrument design, qualitative rigour, and — critically — **an independent data custodian** (see §5). |

**Interpretive `[I]`:** the combination of (longitudinal + cross-degree + new-course pilot + already-instrumented process evidence + sovereign source vault) is unusual enough to be the pitch itself.

