### Three-year projection

**2026-27 — instrument & collect.** Ethics + consent in place before September. Run FE I and FE II with instruments live. FE II *is* the pilot. Deliverable: a clean dataset and a design narrative. **Write nothing for review yet except one experience report.**

**2027 — first outputs.** JENUI 2027 (Spanish, accessible, prize-eligible) + ASSETS 2027 experience report (accessibility strand) + submit the replication study (RQ1) to *Education Sciences* or ITiCSE 2027.

**2027-28 — cycle 2 & consolidation.** Second DBR cycle; longitudinal RQ3 becomes answerable. Target ICER or TOCE with the two-cycle dataset. Propose the RQ5 sequencing paper as design principles.

**Collaboration `[L]`:** **GRIAL / Francisco José García-Peñalvo (Universidad de Salamanca)** `[V]` is the obvious Spanish anchor — an established, indexed, interdisciplinary edtech group. A co-authored replication with a GRIAL member converts a solo practitioner paper into a networked one. Approach after you have data, not before.

